<title>USA: Elan gets FDA approval to market Zanaflex.</title>
<headline>Elan gets FDA approval to market Zanaflex.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elan Corp said its Athena Neurosciences unit received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval to market Zanaflex, an oral drug for treating muscle spasticity, in the U.S.</p>
<p>Zanaflex is expected to be available in U.S. pharmacies in February 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>Elan did not say, however, when it expected the product to contribute to the company's earnings, or how soon that contribution would be.</p>
<p>Elan officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
